  "authoredSolutions": {
    "73": "Tangent to \\(y^{2}=24x\\) at \\((6t^{2},12t)\\) is \\(ty=x+6t^{2}\\). It meets \\(xy=2\\) where \\(ty^{2}-6t^{2}y-2=0\\), so for \\(A,B\\): \\(y_{1}+y_{2}=6t,\\ y_{1}y_{2}=-\\frac{2}{t}\\). The midpoint \\(M\\) has \\(y_{M}=3t\\) and \\(x_{M}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{y_{1}}+\\frac{2}{y_{2}}\\right)=\\frac{y_{1}+y_{2}}{y_{1}y_{2}}=-3t^{2}\\). Eliminating \\(t\\) gives the locus \\(y^{2}=-3x\\), a parabola with latus rectum \\(3\\) and directrix \\(x=\\frac{3}{4}\\), i.e. \\(4x=3\\).",
    "80": "Two edge vectors of the plane are \\((-3,4,-3)\\) and \\((1,-1,1)\\); their cross product gives the normal \\((1,0,-1)\\), so the plane is \\(x-z-1=0\\). The distance of \\((7,-3,-4)\\) is \\(\\frac{|7-(-4)-1|}{\\sqrt{1^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{2}}=5\\sqrt{2}\\).",
    "165": "\\(A\\) lies on the \\(y\\)-axis, which forces \\((\\lambda-2)^{2}=0\\), so \\(\\lambda=2\\), giving \\(A(0,2)\\), \\(AB:3x+2y=4\\) and \\(AC:y=2x+2\\). With orthocentre \\((1,2)\\), the altitude from \\(A\\) is \\(y=2\\) and the altitude from \\(C\\) (slope \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)) meets \\(AC\\) at \\(C\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},1\\right)\\). A tangent from \\(C\\) to \\(y^{2}=6x\\) touches the first-quadrant branch at \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2},3\\right)\\), so its length is \\(\\sqrt{2^{2}+2^{2}}=2\\sqrt{2}\\).",
    "169": "The \\(5\\)-digit numbers use all digits: \\(5!=120\\), and each exceeds \\(7000\\). A \\(4\\)-digit number exceeds \\(7000\\) only when its leading digit is \\(7\\) or \\(8\\): \\(2\\times P(4,3)=2\\times24=48\\). Total \\(=120+48=168\\)."
  },
